%%entity Party help: An organisation participating in freight movements or their settlement. The same organisation can act in several shipment roles without duplicate company records.
%%field Party.name help: Trading name shown in operational lookups; legal document snapshots are kept separately on each job.
%%field Party.code help: Internal customer or supplier account code used to prevent duplicate trading accounts.
%%field Party.legal_name help: Registered name used for contracts, tax invoices and documentary checks.
%%field Party.country_code help: ISO two-letter country of registration used when checking cross-border requirements.
%%field Party.address help: Current registered address; an issued document retains its own historical address snapshot.
%%field Party.email help: Shared operational or accounts mailbox; individual contacts are kept in Contact.
%%field Party.phone help: Main office number for urgent cargo-release or arrival queries.
%%field Party.tax_registration help: GST, VAT or equivalent identifier supplied by the party and checked by finance.
%%field Party.credit_hold help: Finance sets this when new credit or release requires a separate approval.
%%field Party.credit_days help: Agreed number of calendar days used to propose an invoice due date, not a statutory default.
%%field Party.currency_id help: Normal trading currency; individual quotations and invoices may use a different agreed currency.
%%field Party.is_active help: Clear to stop selecting this party for new business while keeping bills and claims readable.
%%section entity: Party; name: Trading identity; help: Match the legal counterparty before accepting cargo or issuing a bill.; rows: name, code | legal_name, country_code | address
