%%entity Quote help: A versioned commercial offer to a customer before a forwarding job is committed. Acceptance fixes a commercial baseline and does not itself guarantee carrier space.
%%field Quote.reference help: Offer reference including revision suffix so a revised price does not overwrite the accepted version.
%%field Quote.party_id help: Customer receiving the offer and expected to approve its scope and exclusions.
%%field Quote.branch_id help: Office issuing the offer and owning the prospective forwarding business.
%%field Quote.owner_id help: Salesperson responsible for obtaining acceptance and explaining exclusions.
%%field Quote.load_type enum: LoadType
%%field Quote.load_type help: fcl prices full containers, lcl prices shared container cargo, and breakbulk covers cargo handled outside standard packed units.
%%field Quote.origin_text help: Quoted collection or loading point, written precisely enough to distinguish port-only from door service.
%%field Quote.destination_text help: Quoted discharge or delivery point defining where the offer’s service ends.
%%field Quote.incoterm enum: Incoterm
%%field Quote.incoterm help: Agreed Incoterms 2020 rule; its named place is recorded separately and it does not replace the forwarding contract.
%%field Quote.named_place help: Place attached to the chosen Incoterm, including terminal detail where risk or cost changes there.
%%field Quote.currency_id help: Single currency used by this offer’s line prices; alternative currency offers require another version.
%%field Quote.valid_until help: Last date on which the customer can accept these commercial rates, subject to stated carrier conditions.
%%field Quote.status enum: QuoteStatus
%%field Quote.status help: quote_draft is editable, quote_offered has been sent, quote_accepted records customer acceptance, and quote_declined or quote_expired closes an unaccepted offer.
%%field Quote.accepted_at help: Time the customer accepted this exact version; empty until acceptance evidence exists.
%%field Quote.terms help: Scope, exclusions, surcharges, rate validity and cancellation conditions given to the customer.
%%field Quote.cost_conversion_rate help: Offer-currency units per supplier-cost currency unit used for converted cost estimates; supporting source currency and dates are retained in the quote terms.
%%section entity: Quote; name: Commercial offer; help: Identify the customer, office and responsibility for this version of the offer.; rows: reference, party_id | branch_id, owner_id
%%section entity: Quote; name: Route and terms; help: Describe the agreed scope before rates are offered.; rows: load_type, origin_text | destination_text, incoterm | named_place, currency_id | valid_until, cost_conversion_rate
%%section entity: Quote; name: Decision; help: Record acceptance or loss without turning the quoted rate into a booking promise.; rows: accepted_at | terms
