%%entity QuoteLine help: One priced service within a quotation. Quantities and prices are kept separately so staff can explain how the offered total was obtained.
%%entity QuoteLine parent: Quote
%%field QuoteLine.quote_id help: Offer version containing this charge; a revised offer has its own lines.
%%field QuoteLine.charge_code_id help: Freight or accessorial service being offered.
%%field QuoteLine.description help: Exact wording and inclusions to show the customer for this service.
%%field QuoteLine.unit_basis enum: UnitBasis
%%field QuoteLine.unit_basis help: Agreed pricing unit for this line, which can override the service’s usual basis.
%%field QuoteLine.quantity help: Number of chargeable units offered, such as containers or revenue tons.
%%field QuoteLine.unit_price help: Net selling rate per chargeable unit in the offer currency.
%%field QuoteLine.minimum_amount help: Minimum net charge applied when quantity multiplied by rate is smaller.
%%field QuoteLine.estimated_cost help: Expected supplier cost for this line in the offer currency at the documented conversion basis.
%%field QuoteLine.conditions help: Rate-specific exclusions, weight-measurement basis or supplier validity conditions.
%%field QuoteLine.cost_basis enum: QuoteCostBasis
%%field QuoteLine.cost_basis help: supplier_quote uses a specific buy offer, tariff uses an identified rate schedule, and converted_estimate uses an explicitly documented source currency and conversion.
%%field QuoteLine.cost_evidence help: Supplier buy-rate reference, source currency and dated conversion basis supporting the estimated cost, so margin assumptions remain reviewable.
