%%entity Shipment help: A customer forwarding job from instruction through delivery and commercial closure. A job can span several carrier bookings, legs and containers.
%%field Shipment.reference help: Internal job number used on handovers, costs and customer progress enquiries.
%%field Shipment.party_id help: Customer commissioning this forwarding service; shipper and consignee are separately recorded as shipment parties.
%%field Shipment.branch_id help: Office accountable for the operational job and its commercial follow-up.
%%field Shipment.owner_id help: Operations coordinator who owns exceptions until this job is closed.
%%field Shipment.quote_id help: Accepted offer version on which this job was sold; leave empty for a separately authorised spot job.
%%field Shipment.customer_reference help: Customer’s purchase order or instruction reference used when matching invoices and cargo.
%%field Shipment.direction enum: Direction
%%field Shipment.direction help: import enters the home market, export leaves it, cross_trade moves between foreign markets, and domestic stays within one market.
%%field Shipment.load_type enum: LoadType
%%field Shipment.load_type help: fcl reserves whole units, lcl shares capacity, and breakbulk travels outside standard packed-container handling.
%%field Shipment.incoterm enum: Incoterm
%%field Shipment.incoterm help: Customer’s agreed Incoterms 2020 rule; confirm the named place and distinguish it from the forwarder’s contracted service.
%%field Shipment.named_place help: Named Incoterm place and relevant terminal detail used to allocate customer and supplier responsibilities.
%%field Shipment.payment_term enum: PaymentTerm
%%field Shipment.payment_term help: prepaid means agreed origin payment, collect means destination collection, and credit means an authorised deferred settlement arrangement.
%%field Shipment.cargo_ready_on help: Customer’s expected date for cargo availability, used when planning collection and carrier space.
%%field Shipment.requested_delivery_on help: Customer’s requested delivery date; an expectation rather than evidence of actual delivery.
%%field Shipment.status enum: ShipmentStatus
%%field Shipment.status help: job_open permits planning, job_booked has carrier arrangements, job_moving is in transit, job_arrived awaits delivery, job_delivered awaits commercial close, and job_closed or job_cancelled ends the job.
%%field Shipment.is_on_hold help: Set while an unresolved safety, document, commercial or regulatory issue prevents the next operation.
%%field Shipment.hold_reason help: Specific unresolved issue and required clearance; do not use a vague note such as pending.
%%field Shipment.cancellation_reason help: Customer or operational reason retained when the job is cancelled rather than deleting its history.
%%section entity: Shipment; name: Job identity; help: Identify the customer order and the office accountable for completing it.; rows: reference, party_id | branch_id, owner_id | quote_id, customer_reference
%%section entity: Shipment; name: Service commitment; help: Record what was accepted rather than assuming every job has identical transport obligations.; rows: direction, load_type | incoterm, named_place | payment_term, cargo_ready_on | requested_delivery_on
%%section entity: Shipment; name: Job progress; help: Move the job only along its operational lifecycle, preserving exceptions in tasks and milestones.; rows: is_on_hold | hold_reason | cancellation_reason
