%%entity CargoItem help: A described cargo lot within a shipment. Package counts and cargo mass describe goods and must not be confused with the packed container’s VGM.
%%entity CargoItem parent: Shipment
%%field CargoItem.shipment_id help: Customer job whose goods are described by this lot.
%%field CargoItem.name help: Recognisable goods description used when selecting the lot for packing and partial delivery.
%%field CargoItem.line_number help: Customer instruction line used to trace this lot across packing lists and allocations.
%%field CargoItem.commodity_code help: Customer-supplied HS classification requiring review by the responsible customs declarant.
%%field CargoItem.package_kind enum: PackageKind
%%field CargoItem.package_kind help: carton, pallet, crate, drum, bag, bundle, piece or tank describes the counted outer handling unit.
%%field CargoItem.package_count help: Number of those outer packages in the whole lot; allocations must not exceed this count.
%%field CargoItem.gross_weight_kg help: Goods and packaging mass in kilograms, excluding the container tare.
%%field CargoItem.net_weight_kg help: Goods-only mass in kilograms where the commercial or customs documents require it.
%%field CargoItem.volume_cbm help: Cargo volume in cubic metres used for LCL planning and W/M pricing.
%%field CargoItem.is_dangerous help: Set whenever the lot requires dangerous-goods assessment; its declarations are recorded separately.
%%field CargoItem.temperature_controlled help: Set for cargo requiring a confirmed temperature-controlled movement.
%%field CargoItem.temperature_celsius help: Requested set point in Celsius; carrier acceptance and operating range require review.
%%field CargoItem.handling_instructions help: Fragility, orientation, segregation or oversize instructions supplied for this specific cargo lot.
