%%entity DangerousGoods help: A dangerous-goods declaration component for a cargo lot. Classification, packing and carrier acceptance need competent review rather than inference from the commodity name.
%%entity DangerousGoods parent: CargoItem
%%field DangerousGoods.cargo_item_id help: Cargo lot containing this declared substance; a lot may contain several classified substances.
%%field DangerousGoods.un_number help: UN identification number including its four digits, checked against the applicable dangerous-goods entry.
%%field DangerousGoods.proper_shipping_name help: Proper shipping name supplied by the competent shipper, including technical name when required.
%%field DangerousGoods.hazard_class enum: HazardClass
%%field DangerousGoods.hazard_class help: Published IMDG class or division from the signed declaration; class_1_1 means 1.1, class_2_1 means 2.1, and the same notation applies to the other divisions. Convert the stored label to the official dotted notation on external documents.
%%field DangerousGoods.subsidiary_risk help: Additional published risk classification where the dangerous-goods entry specifies one.
%%field DangerousGoods.packing_group enum: PackingGroup
%%field DangerousGoods.packing_group help: I denotes high danger, II medium danger, III lower danger, and not_assigned applies only where no packing group is assigned.
%%field DangerousGoods.declared_mass_kg help: Mass attributable to this dangerous-goods component in kilograms, using the declaration’s measurement basis.
%%field DangerousGoods.emergency_contact help: Emergency response contact supplied for transport, reachable during the actual movement.
%%field DangerousGoods.marine_pollutant help: Set when the declared substance meets the applicable marine-pollutant classification.
%%field DangerousGoods.declaration_url help: Location of the signed shipper declaration or its session-authorised evidence record.
%%field DangerousGoods.carrier_accepted help: Set only after documented acceptance for the actual carrier route, not merely after receiving the declaration.
%%field DangerousGoods.imdg_edition help: Edition and amendment of the IMDG rules used by the competent classifier; do not accept an obsolete classification without review.
%%field DangerousGoods.flashpoint_celsius help: Flashpoint in Celsius where required by the declared substance entry; empty where it is not applicable.
%%field DangerousGoods.net_explosive_kg help: Net explosive mass in kilograms where required for the declared explosive entry.
%%section entity: DangerousGoods; name: Declared substance; help: Copy the classification from the shipper’s signed dangerous-goods instruction.; rows: cargo_item_id, un_number | proper_shipping_name, hazard_class | subsidiary_risk, packing_group | imdg_edition
%%section entity: DangerousGoods; name: Acceptance evidence; help: Record the quantity and reviewed evidence before requesting carriage.; rows: declared_mass_kg, emergency_contact | marine_pollutant, declaration_url | carrier_accepted, flashpoint_celsius | net_explosive_kg
%%rbac role:operations|documentation|customs|warehouse|management on DangerousGoods.read
%%rbac role:operations|documentation|customs|warehouse|management on DangerousGoods.create
%%rbac role:operations|documentation|customs|warehouse|management on DangerousGoods.update
%%rbac role:management on DangerousGoods.delete
%%index DangerousGoods(cargo_item_id)

%%entity Booking help: A capacity request to one transport carrier. Confirmation is evidence of carrier acceptance; it is distinct from a customer quotation or a shipment’s delivery promise.
%%field Booking.reference help: Internal booking reference retained even before the carrier issues its own number.
%%field Booking.party_id help: Carrier accepting the requested capacity or equipment.
%%field Booking.voyage_id help: Planned ocean sailing; leave empty until nominated or for an inland-only capacity arrangement.
%%field Booking.carrier_reference help: Number assigned by the carrier, which need not be globally unique across carriers.
%%field Booking.mode enum: Mode
%%field Booking.mode help: ocean, road, rail or barge identifies the carrier service being requested.
%%field Booking.equipment_type_id help: Requested container specification where the carrier provides equipment.
%%field Booking.equipment_count help: Number of requested units; zero is permitted for cargo arrangements without dedicated containers.
%%field Booking.status enum: BookingStatus
%%field Booking.status help: booking_requested awaits response, booking_confirmed holds capacity, booking_amending or booking_cancelling awaits a new carrier decision, and booking_completed, booking_rejected or booking_cancelled is terminal.
%%field Booking.requested_at help: UTC time the request was sent to the carrier, used to trace response delay.
%%field Booking.confirmed_at help: UTC time the carrier accepted the currently confirmed arrangement.
%%field Booking.cargo_cutoff_at help: Carrier cargo acceptance deadline in UTC after converting the nominated terminal’s local time.
%%field Booking.instruction_cutoff_at help: UTC deadline for shipping instructions on this booking.
%%field Booking.vgm_cutoff_at help: UTC deadline the carrier gives for receiving VGM, where applicable.
%%field Booking.confirmation_terms help: Confirmed capacity restrictions and carrier conditions preserved with the booking.
%%section entity: Booking; name: Carrier arrangement; help: Identify the carrier request before linking customer cargo to the reserved capacity.; rows: reference, party_id | voyage_id, carrier_reference | mode, equipment_type_id | equipment_count
%%section entity: Booking; name: Carrier decision; help: Preserve amendments and cancellation requests rather than overwriting confirmed commitments.; rows: requested_at | confirmed_at, cargo_cutoff_at | instruction_cutoff_at, vgm_cutoff_at | confirmation_terms
%%rbac role:sales|operations|documentation|customs|warehouse|finance|management on Booking.read
%%rbac role:operations|documentation|customs|warehouse|finance|management on Booking.create
%%rbac role:operations|documentation|customs|warehouse|finance|management on Booking.update
%%rbac role:management on Booking.delete
