%%entity Allocation help: A portion of a cleared settlement applied to an invoice. Both currency amounts are explicit so foreign-exchange differences never disappear inside a balance update.
%%entity Allocation parent: Settlement
%%field Allocation.settlement_id help: Cleared money movement from which this portion is taken.
%%field Allocation.invoice_id help: Posted invoice whose open balance is reduced or restored by this allocation.
%%field Allocation.status enum: AllocationStatus
%%field Allocation.status help: allocation_draft is proposed, allocation_posted affects balances, and allocation_reversed retains the audit trail while restoring balances.
%%field Allocation.settlement_amount help: Positive amount consumed from the settlement in its own currency.
%%field Allocation.invoice_amount help: Positive amount applied in the invoice’s currency; cannot exceed the remaining authorised balance.
%%field Allocation.conversion_rate help: Invoice-currency units per settlement-currency unit used for this allocation, including an explicit one for same-currency allocation.
